# A method declared with a callable result (T6's `fn: (...) ...` header, code 16) is outside
# the walkable subset (l2_rw_may) -- --walk-methods now refuses it, located, instead of
# silently leaving it native (next_core_tasks.md §7 "Интерпретаторы: те же два примера или
# явное unsupported"; steps/interpreters-callable-parity-t6t7.md). Without the knob this
# translates and runs fine (see unit_make_adder.lm2, the fuller T6 witness); this row only
# exists to pin the --walk-methods refusal text with a minimal reproduction.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    return: addN

add5: makeAdder 5
int: a (add5: 1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: a; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
